Run using Platformio on VSCode
The motor must be plugged into a wall outlet, requires 9V, in order for pump to work.

To run: 
     1. Connect ESP32 to laptop. Upload from platformio onto ESP32.
     2. Connect Motor Controller to power with the power plug.
     3. Close all serial monitors.
     4. Run plot_pulse.py to monitor the plots as they run. At the end of a run, once you close or unplug, the csv will be saved in the /ESP32-V2 folder.

./ESP32-V2/data/: Holds our round one and round two testing
./ESP32-V2/data/...SKIPPED: Holds runs that we removed from final analysis due to poor signal
./ESP32-V2/data/...CLEANED: Holds runs we used for final analysis in round1 and round2

./ESP32-V2/src/: Holds main code for running on ESP32
./ESP32-V2/src/main.cpp: Runs the code
./ESP32-V2/src/config.h: Holds constant variables across project

./ESP32-V2/plot_pulse.py: Run this while connected to the ESP32 to plot PPG and pressure signal in real time. NO SERIAL MONITORS CAN BE OPEN WHEN RUNNING THIS! This include no upload or build terminals. 

./ESP32-V2/csv_test_main.cpp: Runs data analysis remotely. This holds all the code for that to happen on windows. Generates a summary file as well
     - Runs with `.\build_and_run.bat .\INPUT_DATA .\OUTPUT_FOLDER
     - Also a makefile and build file
     
./ESP32-V2/results/: Holds the results of running remotely. Also holds a summary file for each run.

./DataAnalysis.m: Runs all data analysis. At the end, holds plots for the run with k-sounds, pressure, ppg, raw ppg
     - When you run this, will pop up options to add files. Can select as many as you want, then open. This pop up will continue to reopen until you click cancel. This will allow you to add files from different folders if necessary.
     - After running, once it is finished creating the plots at the end (which can take some time), will prompt the user to save a csv file. This csv file holds every run, the auscultatory determined systolic, the oscillatory determined systolic, the visual, and the most confident PPG and the Ensemble PPG results.